   "ladder": "nominal: at rung p each of the two forks carrying a mined positive draws a true nomination with probability p and every other fork a false one, so the realisable true share is at most 0.02 on any rung and no rung claim is adjudicable from this register; the six rungs are six seeded assignments of a false nomination per fork over the same 100 forks, the rule's 'every rung' reads over them as replicate stability, and the precision arm of the hypothesis is carried by the per-session cost = false-nomination change rate x (1 - p), reported; the true-nomination change rate on the mined-positive fork-rungs is a control figure with its count printed, read by nothing",
